<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santa Cruz massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1991</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Dili massacre</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Santa Cruz massacre took place on 12 November 1991, when Indonesian troops opened fire on mourners and pro-independence demonstrators at the Santa Cruz cemetery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dili">Dili</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a>. Estimates of the dead range up to around 250. Filmed by foreign journalists, the killings drew world attention to the Indonesian occupation and strengthened international support for East Timorese self-determination.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santa-cruz-massacre.jpg" alt="Santa Cruz massacre" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Scartol · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sebasti%C3%A3o_Gomes_grave.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
